⏱ 3–8 Minutes — What is a DataFrame?

Let’s start simple.

A DataFrame is a 2-dimensional tabular structure:
	•	Rows → records
	•	Columns → named fields with types

If you’ve used Excel, SQL, or Pandas — same idea.

But here’s the key difference:

In analytics systems, a DataFrame is designed for processing data efficiently, not just storing it.

You can:
	•	Select columns
	•	Filter rows
	•	Join tables
	•	Aggregate
